:::


Then use the below code chunk to add the new statistics into the data frame.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
### The original graph
spark <- report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarize('Monthly Sales' = list(Sales), 
            .groups = "drop")
### The added statistic portion
sales <- report %>% 
  group_by(Product) %>% 
  summarise("Min" = min(Sales, na.rm = T),
            "Max" = max(Sales, na.rm = T),
            "Average" = mean(Sales, na.rm = T)
            )
### Put them together
sales_data = left_join(sales, spark)
```
:::


Finally, plot the graph.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
sales_data %>%
  gt() %>%
  gt_plt_sparkline('Monthly Sales',
                   same_limit = FALSE)
```

